* 04 Zener shunt regulator with the breakdown model: 220 ohm series R, 1N4733A-style 5.1 V Zener, Vin swept 0..20 V.
* Analysis : DC sweep, Vin 0 to 20 V in 50 mV steps (401 rows).
* Outputs  : 04-zener-shunt.csv = vin_V, v_out_V, i_in_A (current from Vin through R into the Zener).
* NODE circuit: Vin -> R 220 -> node out; Zener (cathode = out, anode = gnd), no load.
* Parameters: Zener Is 1e-14 (estimate) N 1 Rs 6.47 BV 5.1 IBV 49 mA NBV 1 (breakdown I = -Ibv*exp(-(Vd+BV)/(NBV*Vt))).
*             ngspice shifts its internal breakdown knee so the current is exactly IBV at Vd = -BV: same law as DESIGN 3.3.
.include common.inc
Vin in 0 0
R1 in out 220
DZ 0 out DZ5V1
.control
dc Vin 0 20 0.05
let i_in = -i(Vin)
set wr_singlescale
set numdgt=8
wrdata build/04.dat v(out) i_in
.endc
.end
